> Closures capture variables, so they see the latest value.
? tf: In Dart, closures created in a `for (var i = 0; ...)` loop all capture the same `i`.
= false
> Each iteration gets a fresh variable, so closures capture 0, 1, 2...
? fill: A function that captures variables from its surrounding scope is called a ___.
= closure
