? scenario: A recursive Fibonacci function takes minutes for n = 45. What is the best fix?
+ Memoise results or rewrite it iteratively
- Add a print statement
- Make n a double
- Increase the stack size
> Overlapping sub-problems make naive recursion exponential; caching fixes it.
? order: Order the lines of a recursive countdown function.
~ void countdown(int n) {
~   if (n < 0) return;
~   print(n);
~   countdown(n - 1);
~ }
> Check the base case first, act, then recurse with a smaller value.
